VISIBLE COMBAT CALCULATION AUDIT — OPTIONAL TEST MODE
This is a temporary diagnostics mode. It changes presentation only, never mechanics.
BUILD RULE: this mode exists only in the separate DEBUG_CALC WorldInfo build, appended to START/PENDING/ACTIVE with one short hard output rule at the top (the v1.23 run loaded the long contract but did not print it). The standard WorldInfo never contains it.

When enabled, every response that initializes, resolves, or ends Combat must make the committed mechanical calculation facts visible to the player in the same response, using the host's ordinary presentation style.
Do NOT reveal hidden chain-of-thought, deliberation, discarded drafts, or private reasoning prose.
Show only authoritative inputs, rolls, arithmetic and committed results.

START / SNAPSHOT FACTS
- semantic phase;
- stable combatant IDs;
- each complete FIXED profile needed for later resolution, including locked Action Library and hostile DefeatXP;
- CURRENT HP/MP/STA/ammo/status and relevant Range Bands;
- Turn Order, Round, Current Actor, Pending trigger/action.

EACH RESOLVED ACTION
- Actor -> Target; action;
- start Range Band; movement transition if any; end Range Band;
- resource/ammo before -> after;
- Hit calculation: Base Hit + explicit modifiers = Final Hit; d100 roll; HIT/MISS;
- Crit chance/modifiers; d100 roll; CRIT/NO CRIT when eligible;
- Raw equation with every scaling term at full precision;
- applicable TOTAL DEF/MDEF and post-defense value;
- Resistance/Weakness if any;
- exact variance;
- Crit multiplier/final modifiers if any;
- final rounded damage; Barrier if any; HP before -> after;
- statuses/effects created/consumed;
- Pending XP change if a target is defeated;
- next Round/Current Actor or terminal state.

COMBAT END
- Defeated/Escaped targets;
- each defeated target's LOCKED DefeatXP;
- Pending XP total;
- persistent XP before -> after;
- any Level-Up loop deltas;
- final semantic phase INACTIVE.

If a value is not applicable, mark it N/A rather than inventing one.
This diagnostics mode never defines XML/tags/block ordering and never overrides the host's existing formatting.
